# KPulla6 Frontend Design Rules

## Product Feel

Design KPulla6 as a premium portfolio analytics dashboard: professional, calm, data-rich, trustworthy.
Closer to institutional wealth analytics than a terminal UI or casual expense tracker.

## Architecture Constraints (non-negotiable)

- React is API-driven — render values from `/api/v1` only.
- Do NOT implement finance calculations in React: no FIFO, XIRR, TWROR, FX conversion, benchmark normalization, or valuation logic.
- Display formatting (currency, percent, axis labels, pie tooltip %) is allowed.
- Preserve existing API contracts unless explicitly requested.
- Do not modify backend or KPulla5.

## Visual System — Institutional Slate

Canonical tokens live in `frontend/src/index.css`. Use these names in new code:

- Backgrounds: `--bg-app`, `--bg-surface`, `--bg-surface-raised`, `--bg-surface-hover`
- Borders: `--border-subtle`, `--border-strong`
- Text: `--text-primary`, `--text-secondary`, `--text-muted`
- Semantic: `--accent`, `--gain`, `--loss`, `--warn`
- Charts: `--chart-1` … `--chart-6`

Use only canonical token names in CSS. Do not introduce legacy `--color-*` or `--font-mono` aliases.

- Cards: elevated surfaces, 8px radius, subtle border/shadow — not hard 1px grid gaps everywhere (later phases).
- Typography: Inter; tabular nums for metrics.
- Restrained palette: accent for controls, green/red ONLY for P/L, amber for warnings.
- Avoid neon terminal colors, pure black backgrounds, decorative gradients.

Full spec: `docs/frontend-design.md`.

## Required Components (Phase 1+ — prefer reuse over one-off markup)

- PageHeader, MetricCard, ChartCard, SectionCard, DataTable
- StatusBadge, WarningBanner, EmptyState
- CurrencyValue, PercentValue, SegmentedControl, Button

Before adding inline styles or new CSS classes on a page, check whether an existing or planned component fits.

## Page layout governance

Before changing any page layout, page structure, or major page-level UI:

1. Read `docs/page-layouts.md`.
2. Propose the layout change in `docs/page-layouts.md` first (use the template there).
3. Mark the proposed change as **Proposed**.
4. Do **not** implement code changes until the user approves the markdown change.
5. After approval: implement the code change, update tests, update `docs/changelog.md`, and mark the layout change as **Implemented**.

Per-page layout spec: `docs/page-layouts.md`.

## Page Rules

### Dashboard
- Performance chart is full-width and visually dominant.
- KPI row above chart; Total Value is the primary metric.
- Group metric, range, and benchmark controls in the chart toolbar.
- Show FX/benchmark warnings near the chart.
- Do not add client-side performance calculations.

### Assets
- Table-first; allocation chart supports the table.
- Closed holdings collapsed by default.
- Numeric columns right-aligned.
- StatusBadge for ok, closed, oversold, price_missing, fx_unavailable.

### Asset Detail
- Tear-sheet layout: hero KPIs, grouped sections, transaction table.
- Breadcrumb to Assets.

### Transactions
- Type badges via `.ui-txn-type`; right-aligned numbers.
- Import errors in WarningBanner-style alert.
- TransactionModal: canonical tokens, modal-local form styles, shared `Button`.

### Settings
- SectionCard layout; explain display currency sync and cached data assumptions.

## Accessibility

- Do not rely on color alone for P/L or status.
- Maintain WCAG-friendly contrast on dark surfaces.
- Preserve aria-labels on portfolio/currency selectors and chart controls.

## Implementation Discipline

- Inspect `frontend/src` before editing.
- Smallest safe change; do not rewrite unrelated pages in one PR.
- Phase 0–8B complete (page migrations, modal cleanup, token cleanup).
- `DataTable` deferred — use page-local table CSS and `.ui-txn-type` for txn types.
- Update frontend tests when UI text, roles, or structure changes.
- Run `make test-frontend` and report results.
